## R-001 — Authenticode Signature Validation Not Enforced

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| **Asset** | WIN11 (domain workstation) |
| **Identified** | July 16–17, 2026 |
| **Status** | In Remediation |
| **Finding** | Windows does not enforce strict Authenticode signature validation by default (CVE-2013-3900 / WinVerifyTrust). An attacker can append malicious content to a legitimately signed file without invalidating its signature — the file still appears validly signed while containing tampered content. |
| **Severity** | High (CVSS 8.8) |
| **Likelihood** | Medium — requires an existing delivery path or foothold; not remotely exploitable on its own |
| **Impact** | High — undermines a foundational OS trust mechanism (code-signing verification) |
| **Treatment** | **Remediate** — enable strict WinVerifyTrust validation via the documented registry-based fix |
| **Residual Risk (post-treatment)** | Low — once enforced, this closes the specific bypass entirely; no known compatibility issues for this environment |
| **Next Review** | Upon remediation completion |
| **Framework Mapping** | NIST CSF: PR.DS-6 (Integrity Checking Mechanisms) · CIS Control 4 (Secure Configuration) |

